    "body": "2026 Paris Motor Show • Project KO11 Is Proof That Geely Wants To \"Knock Out\" Range Rover, Launches Next Year in Europe\nChina-Built Tesla Model 3 Premium Hit With Safety Recall, Over 131,000 Units Affected\n20 photos\nPhoto: Tesla\nThe world's premier electric vehicle manufacturer has issued a recall affecting a bunch of Model 3 Premium sedans produced at Gigafactory Shanghai for three regions. More specifically, the 131,726-strong recall population ended up in the European Union, the Middle East, and South Korea, with said population comprising left-hand-drive sedans exclusively.\nPer the report published via the European Commission's Safety Gate rapid alert system, the far-side airbag software can push shoulder loading past the mandated limit in a side impact. More to the point, recalled vehicles may exceed a lateral force of 3.0 kN on the shoulder during a pole collision.\nBeing a software-only issue, its fix arrives over the air, just as expected from such a tech-infused vehicle. Remedy software changes how the airbag deploys. Tesla calls the campaign SB-26-00-006, which is otherwise known as SR/02850/26 in Safety Gate speak. The regulation at the center of this recall is UN R135, which applies to nearly all new car type approvals worldwide.\nIn said test, a pole strikes the driver's door at 32 kilometers per hour (20 miles per hour), with the driver's seat being occupied by a WorldSID crash test dummy. As noted earlier, the lateral force on the dummy's left shoulder cannot exceed 3,000 Newtons. Under standard Earth gravity, that is the amount of downward force exerted by a 306-kilogram (674-pound) mass. Big yikes!\nNeedless to say, the pole-type side impact is the kind of crash scenario where a narrow object concentrates force into a small area of the door, increasing the risk of injury. Also known as a center or front-center airbag, the far-side airbag was designed specifically to stop the occupant from sliding across the struck area.\nPhoto: Tesla Tesla says it had traced excess load to the software calibration of that airbag's deployment strategy. In other words, the airbag does not deploy in a way that keeps the shoulder loading within the regulatory limit during the pole test. The remedy calibration file is included in software versions 2026.26.100.2, 2026.32.3, or later.\nTesla's own service bulletin, which predated the Safety Gate report, lists Model 3 Premium vehicles produced between June 30, 2024, and May 8, 2026, in left-hand drive at the automaker's Chinese vehicle assembly plant. Service technicians are presented with two correction codes in said bulletin.\nS012600006 means no update is necessary, while S02260006 indicates that the vehicle has to be updated. That being said, the Model 3 continues to live in the shadow of the Model Y as far as worldwide sales are concerned. The real tragedy here isn't that customers prefer crossover, but that the Model 3 is the more efficient and sleeker-looking vehicle of the rear-biased siblings.\nStill one of the highest-volume electric vehicles in the world, the Model 3 carries a starting price of 36,990 euros in Germany for the most basic of specifications. The Model 3 Premium is 44,990 euros from the outset, whereas the Model 3 Performance can be yours from 58,490 before taxes, incentives, and extras.\nWhile it may not be as quick or fast as the Performance, the Premium is the best pick of the bunch in terms of driving range. In the WLTP, it can go up to 750 kilometers (466 miles) on a full charge. Opting for the dual-motor setup results in a WLTP rating of 660 kilometers (410 miles).\nVia // EC Safety Gate\nLiked the article? Follow us to see more articles from autoevolution in your Google feeds.\nTesla Model 3 Tesla recall safety airbag software\nRead Press Release\nAbout the author: Mircea Panait\nAfter a 1:43 scale model of a Ferrari 250 GTO sparked Mircea's interest for cars when he was a kid, an early internship at Top Gear sealed his career path. He's most interested in muscle cars and American trucks, but he takes a passing interest in quirky kei cars as well. Full profile\nUP NEXT 1975 Hurst/Olds Is Dressed To Impress, Packs W30 Power",
